# Workflow: Adopt a pet

1 step, run in order.

## Prerequisites

These variables are referenced by the steps and produced by none of them — set them before running the scenario:

- \`{{pageSize}}\`

## Step 1 — List pets

\`\`\`http
GET https://api.example.com/v1/pets
\`\`\`

Find one that is still available.

Sends:

- Query \`limit\`: \`{{pageSize}}\`

Asserts:

- Status in the \`2xx\` range (the default verdict)

Extracts, under the names the later steps reference as \`{{var}}\`:

- \`petId\` — response body at \`/0/id\`

## Arazzo recipe

\`\`\`json
{
  "arazzo": "1.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Adopt a pet",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "sourceDescriptions": [
    {
      "name": "openapi",
      "url": "https://api.example.com/openapi.json",
      "type": "openapi"
    }
  ],
  "workflows": [
    {
      "workflowId": "adopt-a-pet",
      "summary": "Adopt a pet",
      "inputs": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "pageSize": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "pageSize"
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "stepId": "listpets",
          "description": "Find one that is still available.",
          "operationPath": "{$sourceDescriptions.openapi.url}#/paths/~1pets/get",
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "limit",
              "in": "query",
              "value": "$inputs.pageSize"
            }
          ],
          "successCriteria": [
            {
              "condition": "$statusCode >= 200 && $statusCode <= 299"
            }
          ],
          "outputs": {
            "petId": "$response.body#/0/id"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
\`\`\`

---

# Workflow: Cleanup — Remove a pet

1 step, run in order.

## Prerequisites

These variables are referenced by the steps and produced by none of them — set them before running the scenario:

- \`{{petId}}\`

## Step 1 — DELETE /pets/{petId}

\`\`\`http
DELETE https://api.example.com/v1/pets/{petId}
\`\`\`

Sends:

- Path \`petId\`: \`{{petId}}\`

Asserts:

- Status in the \`2xx\` range (the default verdict)

## Arazzo recipe

\`\`\`json
{
  "arazzo": "1.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Cleanup",
    "version": "3.2.0"
  },
  "sourceDescriptions": [
    {
      "name": "petstore",
      "url": "https://ci.example.com/spec.yaml",
      "type": "openapi"
    }
  ],
  "workflows": [
    {
      "workflowId": "cleanup",
      "steps": [
        {
          "stepId": "drop",
          "operationId": "delete-pets-petid",
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "petId",
              "in": "path",
              "value": "$inputs.petId"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
\`\`\`

---

# List pets

\`\`\`http
GET https://api.example.com/v1/pets
\`\`\`

## Query parameters

- \`limit\` (integer) [max: 100]

## Responses

### 200 — A list of pets

Body \`application/json\`:

- \`id\` (integer, required)

---

# DELETE /pets/{petId}

\`\`\`http
DELETE https://api.example.com/v1/pets/{petId}
\`\`\`

## Path parameters

- \`petId\` (integer, required)

## Responses

### 204 — Deleted
"
